  "slides.1.highlights.0.content": "January 2024 in BC: a plunge below -25°C after 10–13°C days; wind machines work only on calm nights with an inversion; smoke-taint markers are guaiacol and 4-methylguaiacol. Icewine must freeze naturally on the vine (≤ -8°C), is picked at night, pressed frozen and fermented for months; BC requires RS ≥ 100 g/L and VA ≤ 2.1 g/L",
  "slides.1.highlights.1.title": "Industry and market",
  "slides.1.highlights.1.content": "WGC represents about 90% of production; domestic share is about 30% (51% is a goal); exports are led by icewine; in 2018 the Supreme Court rejected full interprovincial free trade; Cellared in Canada was banned from 12 March 2018; economic-impact figures vary, so cite year and source",
  "slides.1.highlights.2.title": "Regulatory history",
  "slides.1.highlights.2.content": "Ontario: voluntary 1988, regulation 1998, VQA Act proclaimed 29 June 2000. BC: began 1990, Reg 79/2005 and the BCWA, replaced by Reg 168/2018; four new GIs in April 2018; the current GI threshold is 85%",
